      "narration": "Some of the richest, most successful people in history have blown up their lives reaching for more they did not even need. They already had money, status, and freedom, and they risked every bit of it to grab a little extra. Housel's point is blunt. There is simply no reason to risk what you have and need, for what you do not have and do not need. Yet that is exactly what people do.",
